      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "DR. ZAIDEN (2) doesn't show much early dash but winds into his races, hitting the line hard to place two back then came home strongly into third (23.98) in a Grade 4/5 at this track last time. Has never missed the frame here at the trip from three starts. Has a strong record from box 2, including two wins. Key chance in this line up. SLAY QUEEN MOLLY (7) has been in the minors the last two, the latest showing strong pace early but gathered in and finished a 1.75 lengths second over 425m this track in 23.94. Although beaten ran one of the quickest times on the card last start. Racing well and deserves a win. JUMBUK WANG WANG (6) was strongly supported last start when a short priced favourite and duly saluted winning by 1.5 lengths at this track in a handy 24.16. Jumping from the pinch draw but goes well over this trip. Leading chance again. PANTHER'S WAY (1) jumps at a shorter trip and still warrants respect.",
